{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Self-Supervised Vision \u2014 SimCLR, DINO, MAE Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Two-view augmentation pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torchvision.transforms as T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "two_view_train = lambda: T.Compose(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T.RandomResizedCrop(96, scale=(0.2, 1.0)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T.RandomHorizontalFlip(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T.ColorJitter(0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 0.1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T.RandomGrayscale(p=0.2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T.ToTensor(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TwoViewDataset(torch.utils.data.Dataset):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, base):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.base = base"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.aug = two_view_train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __len__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return len(self.base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __getitem__(self, i):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        img, _ = self.base[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v1 = self.aug(img)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v2 = self.aug(img)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return v1, v2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each __getitem__ returns two augmented views of the same image; labels are not needed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: InfoNCE loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def info_nce(z1, z2, tau=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    z1, z2: (N, D) L2-normalised embeddings of paired views"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    N, D = z1.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    z = torch.cat([z1, z2], dim=0)  # (2N, D)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = z @ z.T / tau              # (2N, 2N)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = torch.eye(2 * N, dtype=torch.bool, device=z.device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = sim.masked_fill(mask, float(\"-inf\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    targets = torch.cat([torch.arange(N, 2 * N), torch.arange(0, N)]).to(z.device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return F.cross_entropy(sim, targets)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "L2-normalise embeddings before calling. `tau=0.1` is the SimCLR default; lower makes the loss sharper and requires more negatives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Sanity check InfoNCE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "z1 = F.normalize(torch.randn(16, 32), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "z2 = z1.clone()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "loss_same = info_nce(z1, z2, tau=0.1).item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "z2_random = F.normalize(torch.randn(16, 32), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "loss_random = info_nce(z1, z2_random, tau=0.1).item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"InfoNCE with identical pairs:  {loss_same:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"InfoNCE with random pairs:     {loss_random:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Identical pairs should give a low loss (close to 0 for a large batch and cold temperature). Random pairs should give log(2N-1) = ~log(31) = ~3.4 with a 16-pair batch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: MAE-style masking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def random_mask_indices(num_patches, mask_ratio=0.75, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_keep = int(num_patches * (1 - mask_ratio))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    perm = torch.randperm(num_patches, generator=g)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    visible = perm[:n_keep]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    masked = perm[n_keep:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return visible.sort().values, masked.sort().values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "num_patches = 196"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "visible, masked = random_mask_indices(num_patches, mask_ratio=0.75)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"visible: {len(visible)} / {num_patches}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"masked:  {len(masked)} / {num_patches}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Simple, fast, and deterministic for a given seed. Real MAE implementations batch this and keep per-sample masks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Verify that InfoNCE loss drops when you decrease temperature for well-aligned embeddings and rises when you decrease temperature for random embeddings. Produce a plot `tau in [0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.5]` vs loss.\n2. **(Medium)** Implement a DINO-style centre buffer. Show that without the centring, the student collapses to a constant vector within a few epochs.\n3. **(Hard)** Train MAE on CIFAR-100 using the TinyUNet from Lesson 10 as the backbone. Report linear-probe accuracy at 10, 50, and 200 epochs. Show that a MAE-pretrained linear probe beats a from-scratch supervised linear probe on the same 1,000-image subset."
      ]
    }
